From f70652ca1f0aa7e493e5ed534d8be1598c0675f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dini Senanayake <dinindusen@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:55:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Apply the Slurm account and partition to every job

The Slurm executor plugin only reads resources named slurm_account and
slurm_partition, and rules that defined their own resources (salmon quant,
tximeta, the HISAT2 index build, CollectRnaSeqMetrics) did not receive them
at all. Jobs were therefore submitted without an account, relying on each
user's default, and Snakemake logged "No SLURM account given, trying to
guess". On clusters where an account is mandatory these jobs would be
rejected.

- Config templates set slurm_account and slurm_partition under resources:,
  using the plugin's own names. Existing configs with these keys work
  unchanged.
- The CLI reads both values and passes them as --default-resources, so every
  submitted job carries them, including rules with their own resources.
- Workflows drop account/partition keys from the per-rule resources, so the
  CLI value is the only one applied.
- The CLI validates resources.slurm_account; it previously checked
  resources.account, which the templates no longer used.
- Fix the sacctmgr lookups: '$USER' was passed literally (no shell), so
  account validation silently never ran.
- 'txseq <workflow> config' pre-fills the user's default Slurm account; the
  template placeholder is now 'your_slurm_account'.
- Older names (resources.account/partition) are accepted with a warning
  asking for them to be renamed.
- Hold 'threads' separately from the resources dict, and fix hisat.smk
  referring to the removed 'hisat_thread' key.

