 The configuration file is validated before Snakemake is invoked. In
-particular, a valid Slurm account must be set under `resources.account`;
-the run will not start while this is unset or left as the template
-placeholder.
+particular, a valid Slurm account must be set under `resources.slurm_account`;
+the run will not start while this is unset, left as the template placeholder,
+or not one of the accounts associated with your user. When the template is
+written, `slurm_account` is pre-filled with your default Slurm account where
+this can be determined.
+
+```yaml
+resources:
+    threads: 1
+    mem_mb: 1000
+    runtime: 60
+    slurm_account: kir.prj
+    slurm_partition: short
+```
+
+`slurm_account` and `slurm_partition` are the resource names used by the
+Snakemake Slurm executor plugin. txseq passes them to Snakemake as default
+resources (`--default-resources slurm_account=... slurm_partition=...`), so
+every submitted job carries them, including rules that define their own
+memory or runtime. If a workflow is run with `snakemake` directly rather than
+through `txseq`, the same `--default-resources` arguments must be supplied.
+
+Configuration files that use `account` or `partition` (under `resources:` or a
+top-level `slurm:` section) are still accepted; a warning is printed asking
+for the keys to be renamed.
 
 
